-- title:
--   Triviality of residual diamonds at auxiliary level r
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal O$ be a characteristic-zero complete discrete valuation ring (a domain, complete for the adic topology of its maximal ideal) with finite residue field, let $p$ be a prime lying in $\mathfrak m_{\mathcal O}$ and $p \neq 2$. Let $\bar\rho$ be a residual Galois representation over $k=\mathrm{ResidueField}\,\mathcal O$, that is a two-dimensional $k$-vector space $V$ with a monoid homomorphism $\bar\rho.\rho$ from $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q)$ to $\mathrm{End}_k V$ trivial on the subgroup fixing some finite extension of $\mathbb Q$ inside $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, and assume $\bar\rho$ is absolutely irreducible, i.e. its base change to $\overline k$ is irreducible. Let $S$ be a finite set of naturals with $p \in S$, let $N \neq 0$ have all its prime divisors in $S$, and let $r$ be a prime with $r \notin S$ and $r \nmid N$. Let $\theta$ be a ring homomorphism to $k$ from [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N 2 S`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18), the $\mathbb Z$-subalgebra of $\mathrm{End}_{\mathbb C}(S_2(\Gamma_0(N)))$ generated by the $T_\ell$ for primes $\ell \nmid N$, $\ell \notin S$ and the $U_q$ for primes $q \mid N$, $q \notin S$, and assume that for every prime $\ell$ with $\ell \nmid N$, $\ell \notin S$, every valuation subring $P$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $\ell$ a non-unit of $P$, and every $\sigma$ in the decomposition subgroup of $P$ acting on the residue field of $P$ by $x \mapsto x^{\ell}$, one has $\mathrm{charpoly}(\bar\rho.\rho(\sigma)) = X^2 - \theta(T_\ell)X + \ell$. Let $F$ be a field, $\iota : k \to F$ a ring homomorphism, and let $\psi$ be a ring homomorphism to $F$ from the $\mathcal O$-subalgebra of $\mathrm{End}_{\mathcal O}\big(\mathrm{CohCarrier.H1}(Nr, H, \mathcal O)\big)$, with $H = \ker\big((\mathbb Z/Nr)^\times \to (\mathbb Z/r)^\times\big)$, generated by the operators [`CuspForm.AuxLevel.op N r S 𝒪 g`](def/CuspForm_AuxLevelHeckeModule.html#L25) (the Hecke operators $T_{\ell}$ attached to the data $g$ of a prime $\ell \notin S$ with $\ell \nmid N$ and $\ell \neq r$) together with the diamond operators [`CohCarrier.diamondL (N * r) H 𝒪 d`](def/CohCarrier_Inst.html#L55) for $d \in (\mathbb Z/Nr)^\times$ (conjugation by a lift of $d$ to $\Gamma_0(Nr)$). Assume $\psi$ agrees with $\iota \circ (\text{reduction mod } \mathfrak m_{\mathcal O})$ on scalars from $\mathcal O$, and that $\psi$ sends each such $T_\ell$ to $\iota(\theta(T_\ell))$. Then for every $d \in (\mathbb Z/Nr)^\times$, $\psi$ sends the diamond operator at $d$ to $1$.
--
--   This is the residual form of the compatibility between the nebentypus of a weight-two eigenform and the determinant of its Galois representation (Carayol; Darmon–Diamond–Taylor, Theorem 3.1(b)): a character of the Hecke-and-diamond algebra at the auxiliary level $\Gamma_0(N) \cap \Gamma_1(r)$ whose $T_\ell$-values are the Frobenius traces of an absolutely irreducible $\bar\rho$ with cyclotomic determinant has trivial residual nebentypus. It is used in the comparison of the auxiliary level with level $N$, where it shows that the diamond operators act as the identity on the relevant residual eigenspace.
